sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Attendee
    participant Booker as Booker.tsx and useSchedule
    participant SlotsSvc as AvailableSlotsService (slots/util.ts)
    participant OOORepo as PrismaOOORepository
    participant UASvc as UserAvailabilityService
    participant DR as date-ranges.ts
    participant Agg as getAggregatedAvailability.ts
    participant Slots as slots.ts
    participant ATS as AvailableTimeSlots
    participant AT as AvailableTimes
    participant OOO as OOOSlot and OutOfOfficeInSlots
    actor Router as Next.js router

    Note over Attendee,Router: Setup: the host (pro, Europe/London) has an OutOfOfficeEntry from 2:00pm to 4:00pm on Tue Oct 27, not all day, with toUserId set to the forward user

    Attendee->>Booker: open /pro/30min and pick Oct 27
    Booker->>SlotsSvc: trpc viewer.slots.getSchedule (getScheduleHandler, getAvailableSlots)
    Note over Booker,SlotsSvc: Existing code

    SlotsSvc->>OOORepo: getOOODates, findManyOOO(startTimeDate, endTimeDate, allUserIds)
    OOORepo-->>SlotsSvc: OutOfOfficeEntry rows with user, toUser, reason
    SlotsSvc->>UASvc: calculateHostsAndAvailabilities, getUsersAvailability(users, query, initialData.outOfOfficeDays)
    Note over SlotsSvc,UASvc: Existing code

    loop for each host
        UASvc->>DR: getPartialDayOutOfOfficeWindows(outOfOfficeDays, finalTimezone)
        Note over UASvc,DR: New. Skips whole-day entries, parses wall clock with wallClockToTimeZone, lists every host-zone date the window touches
        DR-->>UASvc: PartialDayOutOfOfficeWindow list {dates, start, end, entry}

        UASvc->>UASvc: calculateOutOfOfficeRanges(outOfOfficeDays, availability, partialDayWindows)
        Note over UASvc: Modified. Whole days first, then datesOutOfOffice["2026-10-27"] = {entry data, windows: [{start, end, ...}]}. A whole-day record wins over a window.

        UASvc->>UASvc: calculateHolidayBlockedDates, merge
        Note over UASvc: Modified. A holiday replaces a windowed record but not a whole-day record

        UASvc->>DR: buildDateRanges(availability, timeZone, dateFrom, dateTo, travelSchedules, outOfOffice)
        Note over UASvc,DR: Modified. Dates with windows are not removed from oooExcludedDateRanges as whole days
        DR-->>UASvc: dateRanges, oooExcludedDateRanges

        UASvc->>DR: subtract(dateRanges, busy) and subtract(oooExcludedDateRanges, busy plus windows)
        Note over UASvc,DR: Modified. The window stays in dateRanges and leaves oooExcludedDateRanges (the booking guard reads those)
        DR-->>UASvc: available ranges
    end
    UASvc-->>SlotsSvc: GetUserAvailabilityResult per host {dateRanges, oooExcludedDateRanges, datesOutOfOffice}

    SlotsSvc->>Agg: getAggregatedAvailability(allUsersAvailability, schedulingType)
    Note over SlotsSvc,Agg: Existing. One host uses dateRanges, so 9:00am to 5:00pm stays whole
    Agg-->>SlotsSvc: aggregated DateRange list

    SlotsSvc->>Slots: getSlots(dateRanges, eventLength, frequency, datesOutOfOffice, datesOutOfOfficeTimeZone)
    Slots->>Slots: parseOutOfOfficeWindows(datesOutOfOffice)
    Note over Slots: New. Windows per date parsed to sorted startMs, endMs once per call
    loop for each slot start in buildSlotsWithDateRanges
        Slots->>Slots: findOutOfOfficeForSlot(dayData, windowsOfDay, slotStartMs, slotEndMs)
        Note over Slots: New
        alt date has no record
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time}
        else record without windows (whole day)
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time, away: true, fromUser, toUser, reason, emoji, notes}
        else slotStart before windowEnd and slotEnd after windowStart
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time, away: true, data of the matching window}
        else no overlap with any window
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time}
        end
    end
    Slots-->>SlotsSvc: slots (2:00pm to 3:30pm marked away)
    SlotsSvc-->>Booker: slots grouped by date, with away, fromUser, toUser, reason, emoji, notes
    Note over SlotsSvc,Booker: Existing mapping

    Booker->>ATS: render with scheduleData.slots
    ATS->>ATS: isOOODay = every slot away
    Note over ATS: Modified. Was "first slot away". False here, so the time-format toggle stays
    ATS->>AT: render slots of Oct 27

    alt every slot of the day is away
        AT->>OOO: one OOOSlot for the whole day
        Note over AT,OOO: Existing path, also taken by a window that covers the working day
    else some slots are away
        loop for each slot
            alt slot not away
                AT->>AT: SlotItem (9:00am ... 1:30pm, 4:00pm, 4:30pm)
            else first slot of a run of away slots
                AT->>OOO: OOOSlot with that slot's fromUser, toUser, reason, emoji, notes
                Note over AT,OOO: Modified. One panel per run, placed between the slots before and after the window
            else later slot in the same run
                AT->>AT: skip
            end
        end
    end
    OOO-->>Attendee: away panel: emoji, "Pro Example is OOO", public note

    opt toUser is set on the entry
        OOO-->>Attendee: "Book with Free Example" button
        Attendee->>OOO: click the button
        OOO->>Router: router.push("/free?month=2026-10&date=2026-10-27")
        Note over OOO,Router: Existing code. The redirect only needed toUser on the away slot
        Router-->>Attendee: forward user's booking page on the same date
    end
